684 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 261 0 R
/E (The Project successfully analyzed financial transaction data using Microsoft Excel and Power BI to identify fraud patterns and trends. The data was cleaned, transformed, and visualized through interactive dashboards, enabling analysis based on customer location, merchant category, transaction type, date and fraud status. The use of KPIs, charts, maps, and slicers improved the understanding of transaction behavior and supported effective decision-making. Overall, the project demonstrates how business intelligence tools can transform raw financial data into meaningful insights for fraud monitoring and analysis.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
